    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0084" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1945v01/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/1–1445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leo Pasvolsky, Special Assistant to the Secretary of
                        State, to the Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wright</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-17">January 17, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Michael</hi>: I wish to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note to me, of January 14, 1945,<anchor n="48" xml:id="d5-f1"/> in which
                    you say that His Majesty’s Government is prepared to accept the President’s
                    proposal, as communicated <pb facs="0085" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/> to Prime
                    Minister Churchill on December 5, 1944,<anchor n="49" xml:id="d5-f2"/> with
                    respect to voting in the Security Council of the United Nations Organization.
                    With respect to paragraph 1 of Chapter 8, Section C, the reference is to the
                    second sentence of that paragraph.</p>
                <p>I have been asked to tell you of the gratification which we feel at this
                    indication that the views of our two governments are in accord on this extremely
                    important question.</p>
                <p>We are bearing in mind the points covered in the third paragraph of your note
                    under reference.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leo Pasvolsky</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
